<!-- What Makes a Laptop-Grade Power Bank -->
<section id="what-makes-a-laptop-grade-power-bank" class="sec bg-white relative" data-section="content">
 <div class="container-wide">
 <h2 class="section-title text-center">What Makes a Laptop-Grade Power Bank?</h2>
 <p class="text-center text-slate-500 text-sm max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">Not all power banks can charge laptops. Three technical requirements separate laptop-grade from phone-grade: protocol, capacity compliance, and multi-device delivery.</p>

 <blockquote class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12 bg-brandOrange/5 border-l-4 border-brandOrange rounded-r-xl px-6 py-5 text-sm text-slate-700 italic leading-relaxed">
  <p>"High-capacity power banks (>20,000mAh) specifically designed for laptop charging represent the fastest-growing premium segment, projected to grow at 9.86% CAGR through 2031. The USB-C PD 3.1 standard — enabling up to 240W bidirectional power — is a structural inflection point. With 53 million laptops shipping to the US market annually, laptop power banks are transitioning from niche accessory to essential infrastructure for remote work."</p>
  <cite class="block text-xs text-slate-400 mt-2 not-italic">— <a href="https://www.techsciresearch.com/report/high-capacity-power-banks-market/19744.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">TechSci Research</a>, High Capacity Power Banks Market Report 2025-2031</cite>
 </blockquote>

 <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
 <div class="card-soft p-6 text-center">
 <p class="text-3xl font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">240W</p>
 <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 mb-2">PD 3.1 Protocol</p>
 <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">USB PD 3.1 Extended Power Range (EPR) enables 28V/36V/48V rails up to 240W. Required for gaming laptops and MacBook Pro 16" fast charge at 140W.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="card-soft p-6 text-center">
 <p class="text-3xl font-black text-brandOrange mb-2">100Wh</p>
 <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 mb-2">Airline Compliance</p>
 <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">IATA allows up to 100Wh (27,000mAh @ 3.7V) in carry-on without airline approval. Our 27,000mAh models hit 99.9Wh — maximum capacity, zero travel friction.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="card-soft p-6 text-center">
 <p class="text-3xl font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">2×65W</p>
 <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 mb-2">Dual Port Simultaneous</p>
 <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Charge laptop + phone simultaneously. WOP22 delivers 65W to each USB-C port — enough to power two MacBook Airs at the same time.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

