<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq" class="sec bg-slate-50" data-section="faq">
 <div class="container-narrow">
 {{ sectionHeader('FAQ', 'Laptop Power Bank <span class="text-brandOrange">FAQ</span>', '', {max: ''}) }}
 <div class="reveal">
 {% call faqItem("Can a laptop power bank charge a MacBook Pro?", true) %}Yes. Models with 67W or higher PD output (WOP21, WOP22, WOP23) charge MacBook Pro 13/14/16-inch at full speed. The WOP23 240W PD 3.1 model also supports MacBook Pro 16-inch fast charging at 140W, matching Apple's MagSafe 3 charger output.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("What is PD 3.1 vs PD 3.0?", true) %}PD 3.0 caps at 100W maximum output. PD 3.1 (released 2021) extends the standard up to 240W using new 28V, 36V, and 48V voltage rails (Extended Power Range, EPR). PD 3.1 is required for charging gaming laptops and 16-inch MacBook Pro at full speed.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("Is a 27000mAh laptop power bank airline safe?", true) %}Yes. 27000mAh at 3.7V equals 99.9Wh, just under the 100Wh IATA carry-on limit. All WOWOHCOOL laptop power banks are UN38.3 certified and approved for air carry-on. Anything above 100Wh requires airline approval and is forbidden in checked baggage.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("What is the MOQ for laptop power bank OEM?") %}MOQ starts at 500 units for ODM on in-stock models with custom logo printing. ODM new development: 1,000-2,000 units. OEM with new tooling: 3,000+ units. Sample turnaround: 3-7 days for standard, 10-15 days for custom.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("How long does a 27000mAh power bank charge a MacBook Pro?") %}A 27000mAh (99.9Wh) power bank provides approximately 1.3-1.5 full charges for a MacBook Pro 14" (70Wh battery) or about 0.7-0.8 charges for a MacBook Pro 16" (100Wh battery). With 85% conversion efficiency, expect 85Wh usable energy from a 99.9Wh bank.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("Can I charge a laptop and phone simultaneously?") %}Yes. All WOWOHCOOL laptop power banks support simultaneous multi-device output. The WOP23 can deliver 240W to a laptop while charging a phone via secondary USB-C or USB-A port. Total output is dynamically allocated across ports.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("How do I calculate Wh for airline compliance?") %}Formula: Wh = mAh × Nominal Voltage ÷ 1000. Example: 27000mAh × 3.7V ÷ 1000 = 99.9Wh (just under the 100Wh carry-on limit). Batteries 100-160Wh need airline approval; above 160Wh are prohibited. All WOWOHCOOL models are designed at or below 99.9Wh.{% endcall %}
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

